Z||000006||Formula 18||12-18-2000||10:12 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.justleather.com" TARGET=_blank>www.justleather.com</A> <P>They have full, half, and quarter hides. Plus the have remnates, and bargin hides too.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-19-2000||06:45 PM||||Nothing against real leather, but a high quality vinyl will wear better, last longer, and look nicer than leather and can be purchased for about 1/2 the cost.  I'd like real cow in my GT, but I just might settle for nice plastic.  Nobody will know the difference except me.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever2||12-19-2000||07:11 PM||||The only problem I can think of with that, MM, is vinyl doesn't SMELL like leather.  I don't have leather in my car yet, but Fiero interiors are small, so I would think it would be worth it.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000009||Monkeyman||12-20-2000||05:59 PM||||I've been in some new(er) cars that I would have sworn were lined in leather (smell and all).  Turned out they were one of the better grades of vinyl.  I was as surprised as anyone.  If money were no object, I'd go with all leather in a New York minute, but money's tight...||||reg||1
Z||000010||Daleford||12-20-2000||10:09 PM||||Buying hides and having an upholstery shop do it is exciting.....but when you add it all up would it not be just as cheap to buy the made up leather seat coverings as offered by Mr.Mike or whoever?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000011||Formula 18||12-21-2000||10:12 AM||||It would probally be cheaper to buy Seat cover from Mr Mikes but He doesn't have leather interior parts anymore so that is a problem. It is fairly easy to cover door panels and other flat surfaces so buying hides might be a good option. Like DAD said Vinyl might be a good option too but I have no clue where to get it.<P>Dad's interior look totally sweet but he had his done by a shop if I am correct. I'd like to do a brown and tan interior in a black GT.||||reg||1
